{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000142743249": {
      "title": "Salesforce Opportunities",
      "description": "Griffith University is making a significant, multi-year investment in our Salesforce ecosystem as part of a broader digital transformation strategy. Backed by executive sponsorship and long-term funding, this enterprise-wide program is reshaping how the university engages with students, alumni, staff and the wider community through modern, connected digital experiences. As Griffith continues its transition to a product-led operating model, we are seeking multiple Salesforce professionals to play key roles in this high-profile transformation. Opportunities are available across product management, platform leadership, business analysis, solution architecture, delivery, administration and Salesforce functional specialisations. Why Join? This is far more than a technology implementation. It is a strategic transformation program that will redefine customer engagement, student lifecycle management, advancement and marketing capabilities across the institution. Successful candidates will have the opportunity to: Contribute to a large-scale, enterprise Salesforce transformation. Work within a highly visible program supported by senior executive leadership. Influence strategic decisions that shape the future digital experience of thousands of users. Partner with a diverse range of stakeholders across academic, professional and technology teams. Help establish and mature a product-led culture focused on value, innovation and continuous improvement. Join an organisation committed to investing in modern technologies, people and ways of working. Who We're Looking For We are interested in professionals who bring a combination of Salesforce expertise, strategic thinking and stakeholder engagement skills. Whether your background is in product leadership, platform management, architecture, business transformation or delivery, you'll be passionate about leveraging Salesforce to drive meaningful outcomes and improve customer experiences at scale. Be Part of Something Bigger If you're looking to make a lasting impact through a complex and highly strategic Salesforce transformation program, we'd love to hear from you. This is a unique opportunity to join a forward-thinking organisation and help shape the future of digital engagement in one of Queensland's leading institutions. To explore these opportunities and find out more please reach out to Jason Pretorius, Cox Purtell on  jasonp@coxpurtell.com.au or 049 9141 822",
      "department": "Digital Solutions"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000140590059": {
      "title": "First Peoples Employment Talent Network ",
      "description": "The First Peoples Employment Talent Network provides an opportunity to express your interest in working at Griffith and connect with future employment opportunities across our campuses in both professional and academic areas.  When you apply to join the network, your experience, skills and transferable capabilities will be reviewed to ensure they reflect Griffith's workforce needs. If your application aligns, our First Peoples Employment Partner will contact you to discuss your application.  As a member of the Talent Network, you will be notified of future opportunities that may arise across Griffith's campuses at Brisbane South (Nathan), Gold Coast, Logan and South Bank.  To be considered for this network, candidates should be an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   \n\n Why Join Griffith?  \nAt Griffith, we recognise that employment is about more than a job. It's about belonging, growth, connection and opportunity.  Our  First Peoples Employment Action Plan  is focused on creating the conditions for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees to flourish through cultural safety, leadership development, professional growth, meaningful career pathways and strong community connections. We are committed to ensuring First Peoples staff feel valued, respected and empowered to achieve their career aspirations.   When you join Griffith, you'll become part of a values-led organisation guided by excellence, inclusion, integrity, innovation and reciprocity.    We offer:  A culturally safe and inclusive workplace that values Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and cultures.  Opportunities to connect with other First Peoples staff through dedicated staff networks and community-building initiatives.   Leadership, learning and professional development opportunities designed to support career progression and long-term success.   Flexible work arrangements, including a mix of work-from-home and on-campus options.  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts.  Generous leave provisions, including paid First Peoples Cultural leave, paid parental leave and leave loading.  Support for future study and professional development through Griffith's Educational Staff Assistance Scheme.  Opportunities to contribute to Indigenous-led research, education and community engagement initiatives that create meaningful impact.   You may be an experienced professional, academic, researcher, recent graduate or someone looking to bring your transferable skills into the higher education sector. Through the First Peoples Employment Talent Network, Griffith seeks to build relationships with talented Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are interested in contributing to a university that values Indigenous leadership, knowledge and excellence.   Griffith University values equity, diversity and inclusion. For more information, please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. If you require any accessibility adjustments to submit your application, please contact us. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  \n \n How to apply  \nPlease submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following:  Current curriculum vitae, including name and contact details.  Cover Letter which should be no more than 2 pages in length.  The First Peoples Employment Talent Network is only open to Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander applicants - people who:   a) are of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent; and   \nb) identify as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person; and   \nc) are accepted by their community as being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   Further Information  \nFor further information about the First Peoples Talent Network visit  griffith.edu.au/equity/first-peoples-employment  or contact Bronwyn Horn, First Peoples Employment Partner at  b.horn@griffith.edu.au . You can also stay up to date with all recruitment activity at Griffith via our  First Peoples Employment at Griffith LinkedIn  group.   \n\n Join Griffith University and be part of a community where Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are supported to flourish.  At Griffith, we are committed to creating the conditions for First Peoples staff to thrive. We aspire to be the university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples by fostering a culturally safe workplace, supporting career growth and leadership, celebrating Indigenous knowledges, and creating meaningful employment opportunities across the University.",
      "department": "Corporate Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000140589949": {
      "title": "First Peoples Employment Talent Network",
      "description": "The First Peoples Employment Talent Network provides an opportunity to express your interest in working at Griffith and connect with future employment opportunities across our campuses in both professional and academic areas.  When you apply to join the network, your experience, skills and transferable capabilities will be reviewed to ensure they reflect Griffith's workforce needs. If your application aligns, our First Peoples Employment Partner will contact you to discuss your application.  As a member of the Talent Network, you will be notified of future opportunities that may arise across Griffith's campuses at Brisbane South (Nathan), Gold Coast, Logan and South Bank.  To be considered for this network, candidates should be an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   \n\n Why Join Griffith?  \nAt Griffith, we recognise that employment is about more than a job. It's about belonging, growth, connection and opportunity.  Our  First Peoples Employment Action Plan  is focused on creating the conditions for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees to flourish through cultural safety, leadership development, professional growth, meaningful career pathways and strong community connections. We are committed to ensuring First Peoples staff feel valued, respected and empowered to achieve their career aspirations.   When you join Griffith, you'll become part of a values-led organisation guided by excellence, inclusion, integrity, innovation and reciprocity.    We offer:  A culturally safe and inclusive workplace that values Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and cultures.  Opportunities to connect with other First Peoples staff through dedicated staff networks and community-building initiatives.   Leadership, learning and professional development opportunities designed to support career progression and long-term success.   Flexible work arrangements, including a mix of work-from-home and on-campus options.  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts.  Generous leave provisions, including paid First Peoples Cultural leave, paid parental leave and leave loading.  Support for future study and professional development through Griffith's Educational Staff Assistance Scheme.  Opportunities to contribute to Indigenous-led research, education and community engagement initiatives that create meaningful impact.   You may be an experienced professional, academic, researcher, recent graduate or someone looking to bring your transferable skills into the higher education sector. Through the First Peoples Employment Talent Network, Griffith seeks to build relationships with talented Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are interested in contributing to a university that values Indigenous leadership, knowledge and excellence.   Griffith University values equity, diversity and inclusion. For more information, please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. If you require any accessibility adjustments to submit your application, please contact us. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  \n \n How to apply  \nPlease submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following:  Current curriculum vitae, including name and contact details.  Cover Letter which should be no more than 2 pages in length.  The First Peoples Employment Talent Network is only open to Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander applicants - people who:   a) are of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent; and   \nb) identify as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person; and   \nc) are accepted by their community as being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   Further Information  \nFor further information about the First Peoples Talent Network visit  griffith.edu.au/equity/first-peoples-employment  or contact Bronwyn Horn, First Peoples Employment Partner at  b.horn@griffith.edu.au . You can also stay up to date with all recruitment activity at Griffith via our  First Peoples Employment at Griffith LinkedIn  group.   \n\n Join Griffith University and be part of a community where Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are supported to flourish.  At Griffith, we are committed to creating the conditions for First Peoples staff to thrive. We aspire to be the university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples by fostering a culturally safe workplace, supporting career growth and leadership, celebrating Indigenous knowledges, and creating meaningful employment opportunities across the University.",
      "department": "Corporate Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000140111718": {
      "title": "First Peoples Employment Talent Network",
      "description": "The First Peoples Employment Talent Network provides an opportunity to express your interest in working at Griffith and connect with future employment opportunities across our campuses in both professional and academic areas.  When you apply to join the network, your experience, skills and transferable capabilities will be reviewed to ensure they reflect Griffith's workforce needs. If your application aligns, our First Peoples Employment Partner will contact you to discuss your application.  As a member of the Talent Network, you will be notified of future opportunities that may arise across Griffith's campuses at Brisbane South (Nathan), Gold Coast, Logan and South Bank.  To be considered for this network, candidates should be an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   \n\n Why Join Griffith?  \nAt Griffith, we recognise that employment is about more than a job. It's about belonging, growth, connection and opportunity.  Our  First Peoples Employment Action Plan  is focused on creating the conditions for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees to flourish through cultural safety, leadership development, professional growth, meaningful career pathways and strong community connections. We are committed to ensuring First Peoples staff feel valued, respected and empowered to achieve their career aspirations.   When you join Griffith, you'll become part of a values-led organisation guided by excellence, inclusion, integrity, innovation and reciprocity.    We offer:  A culturally safe and inclusive workplace that values Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and cultures.  Opportunities to connect with other First Peoples staff through dedicated staff networks and community-building initiatives.   Leadership, learning and professional development opportunities designed to support career progression and long-term success.   Flexible work arrangements, including a mix of work-from-home and on-campus options.  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts.  Generous leave provisions, including paid First Peoples Cultural leave, paid parental leave and leave loading.  Support for future study and professional development through Griffith's Educational Staff Assistance Scheme.  Opportunities to contribute to Indigenous-led research, education and community engagement initiatives that create meaningful impact.   You may be an experienced professional, academic, researcher, recent graduate or someone looking to bring your transferable skills into the higher education sector. Through the First Peoples Employment Talent Network, Griffith seeks to build relationships with talented Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are interested in contributing to a university that values Indigenous leadership, knowledge and excellence.   Griffith University values equity, diversity and inclusion. For more information, please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. If you require any accessibility adjustments to submit your application, please contact us. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  \n \n How to apply  \nPlease submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following:  Current curriculum vitae, including name and contact details.  Cover Letter which should be no more than 2 pages in length.  The First Peoples Employment Talent Network is only open to Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander applicants - people who:   a) are of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent; and   \nb) identify as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person; and   \nc) are accepted by their community as being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   Further Information  \nFor further information about the First Peoples Talent Network visit  griffith.edu.au/equity/first-peoples-employment  or contact Bronwyn Horn, First Peoples Employment Partner at  b.horn@griffith.edu.au . You can also stay up to date with all recruitment activity at Griffith via our  First Peoples Employment at Griffith LinkedIn  group.   \n\n Join Griffith University and be part of a community where Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are supported to flourish.  At Griffith, we are committed to creating the conditions for First Peoples staff to thrive. We aspire to be the university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples by fostering a culturally safe workplace, supporting career growth and leadership, celebrating Indigenous knowledges, and creating meaningful employment opportunities across the University.",
      "department": "Corporate Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000120831317": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarships: Machine Vision",
      "description": "This research aims to advance knowledge of machine vision for deep visual understanding of natural objects and environments. The primary focus of this role is to undertake fundamental research in visual understanding and multimodal machine learning. Research activities include developing novel deep learning methods for representation learning, vision-language reasoning, fine-grained and ultra-fine-grained visual categorization, and trustworthy AI systems. The candidate will publish high-quality research papers in leading conferences and journals in computer vision and machine learning. Successful candidates will have the opportunity to receive advanced research training and work within a vibrant research environment that includes a team of research fellows, industry collaborators, and PhD students. The position provides opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers and participation in international research communities in computer vision, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of academic merit and research background. To be successful in this role, you should demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving skills, solid mathematical foundation, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a research environment. Evidence of a passion for computer vision and image processing is essential. Previous experiences in deep learning, visual recognition, multimodal AI, pattern recognition, or data-driven modelling are preferred. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to  first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer  here . Please note : Applicants with academic qualifications in computer science, engineering, applied mathematics, with a publication record in top tier venues such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, AAAI, IJCAI are preferred. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 OR A score of no less than 3+ in each skill of the ISLPR (conducted by ISLPR Language Services only) OR A minimum overall score of 176 (no score less than 169) on C1 Advanced  or  C2 Proficiency OR An overall score of 58 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 50 (applies to tests taken prior to 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 55 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 47 (applies to tests taken on or after 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 70 in the LanguageCert Academic OR An overall score of 59 in the Michigan English Test (MET) . \n\n About the scholarship \nThe successful candidate will be awarded a Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUPRS) or an equivalent scholarship package funded through the ARC Industry Laureate Fellowship. \n \nThe 2026 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $35,656 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the GUPRS Conditions of Award for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the GUIPRS Conditions of Award for more information. \n \n EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to yongsheng.gao@griffith.edu.au, containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Brief research proposal, maximum 2 pages Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is: Currently Open  The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line \n \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Yongsheng Gao \nEmail:  yongsheng.gao@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n We are currently looking for 4 highly motivated PhD candidates to join the research of “Next-Generation Visual Understanding” funded by the ARC Industry Laureate Fellowship. The successful candidate will join the research team led by an Australian Industry Laureate Fellow and internationally recognized researchers in smart farming, computer vision, machine learning, and artificial intelligence, within the School of Engineering and Built Environment at Griffith University. The research environment is collaborative and multidisciplinary, combining expertise in deep learning, computer vision, data science, and applied AI, and working closely with industry partners, national research institutions, and international collaborators. \n \nThis opportunity will be primarily based at the Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000071420565": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship:  Validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis",
      "description": "We are currently seeking highly motivated PhD candidates to join our research team at Griffith University. This exciting project aims to develop and validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis. Highlights of working on this project include: Focus on non-invasive, saliva-based diagnostics for liver fibrosis. Integration of clinical collaboration with hospital partners and cutting-edge research in the laboratory. Opportunity to work at the intersection of translational medicine, proteomics, and biomarker development. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful in this role, you should have: A strong academic background in Medical Laboratory Science, Pathology, Molecular Pathology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience working at the interface with hospital laboratories and working with clinicians. Evidence of collaborative skills and the ability to work effectively with clinical and laboratory-based research teams. A clear passion for research and a commitment to advancing the field of liver fibrosis paving the way for precision health. Should hold a valid Australian driver's licence. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to  first  class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Procedure .  For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer  here . Please note : Applicants must have obtained a Master’s degree or an Honours degree in relative fields. A solid background in Medical Laboratory Science, Pathology, Molecular Pathology with an interest in biomarker discovery is required. Some experience in the field of multivariate statistical analysis would be beneficial but is not required. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 \n\n About the scholarship \nThe 2025 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $34,752 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  c.punyadeera@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section, including a  copy of your academic transcript A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names of  two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is:  Tuesday 29 July 2025 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Chamindie Punyadeera \nEmail: c.punyadeera@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n The Saliva and Liquid Biopsy Group is dedicated to advancing biomarker discovery for metabolic diseases and cancer, with the goal of improving precision health. Our research focuses on identifying and validating biomarkers that enable more accurate patient stratification based on disease risk, prognosis, and treatment response. The successful PhD applicant will be based at the Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics (IBG), Griffith University, Brisbane South (Nathan) and will work within a collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000040674965": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship:  Synthetic biopolymer-protein conjugates for enhanced mucosal delivery of drugs and antigens",
      "description": "We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to develop innovative biopolymer-protein conjugates for enhanced mucosal delivery of drugs and antigens. This will include electrohydrodynamic atomisation for nasal delivery. The primary focus of this role is to design and develop functional biopolymers that target the mucosa and that are amendable toward electrohydrodynamic atomisation to overcome the current drug and antigen delivery limitations. The project aims to enhance the efficacy of biopolymer micro/nanoparticles through precise control of particle size and charge and fill the gap between the fast advancement in nasal drug and vaccine discovery and conventional ineffective delivery techniques. Success in this role requires knowledge in design of functional polymer particles, generation of cell factories as production strains, bioprocess development and characterisation of nanomaterials before and after the nebulising process. \n  \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful within this role, you will be able to work in bioengineering, microfluidics, and material science. You will have evidence of a passion for conducting high impact research, with strong desire to undertake research in multidisciplinary research. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to  first  class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Procedure .  For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer  here . Please note : You should have strong background in Material/Biomaterial science and experiences in design, analysis, fabrication and characterization of new material samples. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 \n  \n\n About the scholarship \nThe 2025 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $34,752 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. \n \n EoI process \nPlease do not  select the “I'm Interested” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  v.dau@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section, including a  copy of your academic transcript A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names of two referees Closing date of expressions of interest: Friday 7 March 2025 at 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship online. \n \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across locations in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nDr Van Dau \nEmail:  v.dau@griffith.edu.au \n \nProfessor Bernd Rehm \nEmail:  b.rehm@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n Working for one of the most influential universities in Australia and the Asia–Pacific region, you will join a University that spans five physical locations in South East Queensland and all disciplines, while our network of more than 200,000 graduates extends worldwide. We have world-class facilities for micro- and nanotechnology and advanced manufacturing. You will conduct the advanced research at the Centre for Cell Factories and Biopolymers, the centre equipped with modern bioprocessing equipment, including cell disruptors, homogenisers, bioreactors, and chromatography system. It is also located in a PC2 laboratory which is equipped with an array of instruments that enable synthetic biology of bacterial production strain. This opportunity will be primarily based at Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149768069": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Level B) in Midwifery",
      "description": "Griffith University Lecturer (Level B) in Midwifery | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer (Level B) in Midwifery Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Logan Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Nursing and Midwifery - Midwifery - MID Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description At Griffith University we believe in, strive for and celebrate the remarkable. We are known for our high impact research, outstanding student experience, our commitment to social justice and our welcoming environment. We rank in the top 2% of universities worldwide and we’re proud of our remarkable achievements, of our people and their passion for making a positive difference. Together we contribute to the development of knowledge and learning in an attractive environment which values excellence, equity, diversity, and innovation. The School of Nursing and Midwifery is one of the largest of schools at Griffith University. Our School has a strong reputation, and we are committed to the global development of nursing and midwifery practice, theory and research in positive and visionary ways. Through developing research, consultancy and continuing education opportunities, we seek to serve the nursing and midwifery professions, the healthcare system and the broader community. This is your opportunity to contribute to our leading midwifery programs and to part of an innovative and progressive team. The Midwifery programs and staff uphold a values-based framework that includes being woman-centred and promoting and privileging midwifery continuity of care. Job Description The School is seeking to appoint a Lecturer (Level B) Midwifery in a teaching focused role, where you will undertake teaching, course coordination and curriculum development. You are expected to have demonstrated clinical midwifery expertise and teaching experience. You will also undertake some learning and teaching research or scholarship. If eligible, supervision of Honours and research higher degree student is possible. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Logan. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. Qualifications To be successful in this role you will have: Registration with Australian Health Practitioner Regulatory Agency (Ahpra) as a registered midwife. A minimum of a Masters qualification in midwifery (or equivalent). Previous midwifery teaching experience in the tertiary sector. Highly desirable is Ahpra endorsement for scheduled medication for midwives. Desirable completion of or enrolment in doctoral level program in midwifery or relevant field. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner, Head of School at [email protected] For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] Closing date: Tuesday 20th October at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000151300389": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Oral Surgery",
      "description": "Griffith University Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Oral Surgery | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Oral Surgery Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of MDP - Dentistry and Oral Health - DOH Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Medicine and Dentistry strives to prepare the next generation of professionals and practitioners to tackle health and healthcare challenges in an ever-changing world. As a community, we are committed to building better health outcomes for all by delivering high-quality education, impactful research and engagement with and for the communities we serve. As articulated in our Strategic Plan, we commit to the University's values and, importantly, to being a School for Country, place, communities and the people we serve. Through our learning and teaching, we strive to produce graduates who are confident, competent and resilient to be agents for change. We are committed to recruiting and retaining the best possible staff; staff who support our educational mission to deliver an outstanding student learning experience and producing competent, compassionate health professional and practitioners. The School of Medicine and Dentistry shares the Health Group and broader University's commitment to excellence, ethical behaviour, and engagement. The Health Group Charter articulates the core values and behaviours we expect in our workforce: inclusion, integrity, performance, respect, and collaboration.  These values and behaviours are embedded in the School's annual Academic Employee Career Development (AECD) / Professional Staff Career Development (PSCD) process and frame staff performance planning and review conversations. Job Description We are seeking qualified candidates for the role of Lecturer (Level B) / Senior Lecturer (Level C) in Oral Surgery. The successful candidate will be expected to make significant contributions to the clinical and didactic teaching effort of the School of Medicine and Dentistry and play a major role in scholarship, research and/or professional activities. The incumbent will promote and support the School’s educational mission in relation to dentistry and oral health. They will contribute to the development and implementation of high-quality learning and assessment activities across courses and programs. The incumbent will also contribute to the broader mission of the School through scholarly and service activities as negotiated with their supervisor. This is a full-time continuing role based at our Gold Coast location. As Griffith is a multi-campus institution, there may be some requirement to attend other campuses on occasion. There is a requirement for considerable face-to-face didactic and clinical teaching, so the expectation is that the incumbent will regularly attend campus across the extended dentistry academic calendar, contributing to learning and teaching, research/scholarship and service activities to support the discipline and the School more broadly. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. The full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level C range $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Qualifications Candidates seeking appointment at Lecturer (Level B) will be expected to possess: A postgraduate qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent accreditation and standing, and/or significant progress towards completion of a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline or field. Current registration or eligibility for registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra). The demonstrated ability to teach and supervise students primarily in Oral Surgery. Evidence of research, scholarship, or professional engagement. Clinically active in professional practice. Candidates seeking appointment at Senior Lecturer (Level C) will be expected to possess: A postgraduate qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent accreditation and standing, and either a doctoral qualification (PhD) or equivalent academic, clinical, or professional standing. Current registration or eligibility for registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Evidence of experience in the delivery of student learning and curriculum development, including teaching and supervision in Oral Surgery. An established record of research and scholarship, with the potential to establish a grant-funded program of research. Evidence of ability to mentor HDR candidates on dissertation projects. Clinically active in professional practice. Evidence of academic or professional leadership. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission). Visa sponsorship may be available to the successful candidate. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Donald Chi, Dean of Dentistry at [email protected] . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Tuesday, 3 November 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000151295019": {
      "title": "Griffith University General Dentist",
      "description": "Griffith University General Dentist – Warwick, Queensland | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . General Dentist – Warwick, Queensland Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Off Campus Location Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: GHC - Private Practice Suites - IPP Appointment Type: Fixed Term Job Description General Dentist – Warwick, Queensland Make a real impact in regional Australia while enjoying an outstanding work-life balance! Are you a passionate General Dentist looking for a role where you can focus on quality patient care, mentor the next generation of dentists, and enjoy a lifestyle that leaves your weekends free? Griffith University is seeking a General Dentist to join our modern dental clinic in Warwick, Queensland, on a 5-year fixed-term contract. This is a unique opportunity to combine clinical practice with teaching in a supportive, collaborative environment without the pressures of private practice ownership or weekend work. Why join us? Salary of $170,000 – $190,000 base plus 17% superannuation (commensurate with experience) Monday to Friday – no weekend work 5-year fixed-term appointment offering long-term stability Work alongside an experienced and supportive academic and clinical team Help shape the future of dentistry by mentoring final-year dental students About the role Based at the Griffith University Dental Clinic in Warwick, you'll provide high-quality general dental care while playing an important role in educating Griffith's fifth-year dental students. During teaching periods, you'll supervise students delivering comprehensive patient care across a broad range of dental disciplines, helping them build the confidence and clinical skills they need for professional practice. Outside teaching periods, you'll focus on providing exceptional general dental care to patients from the Warwick and Granite Belt communities. This role offers the best of both worlds; clinical practice combined with education in a collaborative university environment. About you We're looking for someone who: Is registered as a General Dental Practitioner with Ahpra Has experience practising as a dentist in Australia (a minimum of two years is desirable) Has a genuine passion for providing outstanding patient care Enjoys mentoring and supporting developing clinicians Has excellent communication and interpersonal skills Values collaboration, professionalism and continuous learning Is excited about becoming part of the Warwick community Has an interest in supervising and mentoring dental students, with previous student supervision experience highly regarded but not essential. Why Warwick? Located just two hours from Brisbane, Warwick offers an exceptional regional lifestyle with affordable living, excellent schools, welcoming communities and easy access to the beautiful Granite Belt wine region and national parks. Whether you're looking to escape the city commute, relocate with your family, or simply enjoy more balance in your life, Warwick offers the opportunity to build both a rewarding career and a great lifestyle. About Griffith University Griffith University is one of Australia's leading universities, recognised for innovation, teaching excellence and creating meaningful community impact. Our Dental Clinics provide high-quality patient care while supporting the education of future oral health professionals. Joining our team means becoming part of a collaborative culture that values excellence, integrity, compassion and lifelong learning. If you're looking for a role where your clinical expertise will have a lasting impact on both patients and the next generation of dentists, we'd love to hear from you. Additional Information How to apply At Griffith, we're committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming environment for everyone. If you require any adjustments throughout the recruitment process, please let us know so we can support your participation. We value diversity, inclusion and flexibility, and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and people of all backgrounds. For more information, please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . To be considered for this opportunity, please submit your application online and include: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the position description and eligibility requirements). A current curriculum vitae/resume, including your full contact details. The names and contact details of at least three professional referees (referees will not be contacted without your permission). Please note: Applicants must have unrestricted working rights in Australia. Unfortunately, visa sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information about the role, please contact Dr Megan Gray, Clinical Director, Dental Clinic, at megan.gray@griffith.edu.au . For recruitment and application enquiries, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner, at j.dhall@griffith.edu.au . We encourage you to submit your application as soon as possible, as applications will be reviewed as they are received. Apply today and discover a rewarding career with Griffith University in beautiful Warwick, Queensland. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Associate Lecturer (Level A) Occupational Therapy Nathan, Australia Information Solutions Analyst Nathan, Australia Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Oral Surgery Southport, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. General Dentist – Warwick, Queensland 56 Locke St, Warwick QLD 4370, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000151536339": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Level C) Social Work (Field Education Lead)",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Lecturer (Level C) Social Work (Field Education Lead) | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Senior Lecturer (Level C) Social Work (Field Education Lead) Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Logan Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of SHS - Human Services and Social Work - HSV Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Shape future social workers. Live the Queensland lifestyle. Be part of Brisbane 2032. As Southeast Queensland prepares for the world stage with the Brisbane 2032 Olympic and Paralympic Games, Griffith University is investing in people who want to make a lasting impact — locally, nationally and globally. We are seeking an inspiring Field Education Lead in Social Work to join our School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work within Griffith Health. This is a rare opportunity to combine high-impact teaching, applied professional practice, impactful research, and a rewarding academic career with one of Australia’s most enviable lifestyles. Why Griffith? Griffith University is recognised globally for its commitment to social justice, innovation, and transformational education. Ranked in the top 2% of universities worldwide, we are proud of our people, our culture, and our focus on producing work-ready graduates who make a difference. The School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work is known for excellence in health and human services education, with strong connections to industry, community partners, and the Social Work profession. We have strengths in domestic and family violence, child and family wellbeing, mental health, disability, community practice, ethics, applied social work interventions, and social work research methods. Job Description As a Senior Lecturer (Level C), you will play a key role in shaping the next generation of social workers through innovative, student-centered, and practice-informed teaching. We are especially interested in candidates with the expertise to lead the large field education program across the BSW and MSW.  Reporting to the Academic Lead for Social Work and Human Services and working closely with the WIL Placement Manager and team, the role will build on the existing placement partnerships, systems and processes required to support high-quality professional placements. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to build on current and establish new sustainable placement models while also contributing to teaching and research in the discipline. In this role you will: Build and manage industry placement partnerships across health, community, government and related sectors. Coordinate all aspects of student placements, including preparation, matching, support, monitoring and assessment. Ensure placement compliance through effective policies, procedures, records and regulatory requirements. Provide expert stakeholder engagement and guidance, resolving complex placement and student matters. Deliver high-quality teaching, applied learning, research and industry partnerships to enhance student employability and support future growth. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at either Griffith University Gold Coast or Logan. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level C range $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Qualifications You are a passionate social work educator who thrives on developing capable, reflective, and ethical graduates. You will bring: A doctoral or masters qualification (or equivalent accreditation and standing with significant professional experience) in Social Work or a related field Eligibility for membership of the AASW Demonstrated expertise of at least five years in one or more applied fields of practice as well as field education experience A strong commitment to practice-informed, student-centred teaching Experience coordinating courses and contributing to program quality and accreditation Excellent interpersonal skills and an ability to work collaboratively and embody the values and behaviours that include collegiality and respectful interprofessional practice and engagement Please note, applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders are strongly encouraged. Additional Information Why Griffith? Based in South East Queensland, this role offers more than a career; it offers a way of life. Experience a vibrant and fast-growing region as it prepares for the Australian Association of Social Workers (AASW) 2026 Social Work Congress on the Gold Coast in November, and the Brisbane 2032 Olympic and Paralympic Games. Enjoy effortless access to worldclass beaches and stunning hinterland, complemented by a relaxed outdoor lifestyle, excellent schools, high-quality healthcare, and strong connectivity. Griffith University’s campuses across the Gold Coast, Logan and Brisbane foster strong professional networks and a deeply connected academic community. If you are ready to educate for impact, contribute to a values-led university, and build a meaningful academic career while enjoying an exceptional lifestyle, we would love to hear from you. Apply now and join us in shaping the future, advancing outcomes for our students, strengthening communities, and contributing to social work in Queensland, on the national and international stage. How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Associate Professor Jennifer Smith, School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work at [email protected] For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] Closing date: Sunday, 25 October at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000152320829": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Clinical Education Phase 2 and 3 Lead, Doctor of Medicine",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Clinical Education  Phase 2 and 3 Lead, Doctor of Medicine  | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Clinical Education  Phase 2 and 3 Lead, Doctor of Medicine Part-time Primary Location (Campus): Sunshine Coast University Employment Type: Part Time Department ID: School of MDP - Clinical Medicine Sunshine Coast - CMS Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Medicine and Dentistry strives to prepare the next generation of professionals and practitioners to tackle health and healthcare challenges in an ever-changing world. As a community, we are committed to building better health outcomes for all by delivering high-quality education, impactful research and engagement with and for the communities we serve. As articulated in our Strategic Plan, we commit to the University's values and, importantly, to being a School for Country, place, communities and the people we serve. Through our learning and teaching, we strive to produce graduates who are confident, competent and resilient to be agents for change. We are committed to recruiting and retaining the best possible staff; staff who support our mission and vision to deliver an outstanding student learning experience and producing competent, compassionate health professional and practitioners. The School of Medicine and Dentistry shares the Health Group and broader University's commitment to excellence, ethical behaviour, and engagement. The Health Group Charter articulates the core values and behaviours we expect in our workforce: inclusion, integrity, performance, respect, and collaboration.  These values and behaviours are embedded in the School's annual Academic Employee Career Development (AECD) / Professional Staff Career Development (PSCD) process and frame staff performance planning and review conversations. Job Description We are seeking an enthusiastic, clinically active medical practitioner to deliver clinical education of medical students in Phases 2 and 3 of the MD program based at the Sunshine Coast Health Institute and Sunshine Coast University Hospital, comprising the final two clinical years of the four-year curriculum. This will include coordinating the simulation and case-based learning, bedside teaching and assessment; and where needed, provision of academic support for students undertaking Phases 2 and 3 of the program. In this position, the successful candidate will be expected to make significant contributions to the teaching effort of the School of Medicine and Dentistry, as well as playing a major leadership role in the teaching, assessment, course convenorship and curriculum development activities relevant to the Doctor of Medicine (MD) program. In addition, they will provide academic leadership to foster teaching innovations and excellence in scholarship, service and/or professional activities. Additionally, the position will also involve collaboration with the Clinical Sub-Dean of Sunshine Coast Hospital as well as other Phase Leads and academic colleagues across the campuses and sites at which the medical program is delivered to ensure a consistent, high-quality student learning experience. This is a part-time (20% / 0.2FTE), continuing role based at the Sunshine Coast Health Institute and Sunshine Coast University Hospital. The level of appointment will be contingent upon the educational and professional qualifications and experience. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary for an Academic Senior Lecturer (Level C) will range from $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will range from $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. The full time equivalent base salary for an Academic Associate Professor (Level D) will range from $172,686 - $190,248 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will range from $202,043 - $222,590 per annum. Qualifications We are seeking applications from candidates who: Possess a medical degree from a recognised educational institution. Possess of a PhD or equivalent qualification in an appropriate discipline, or evidence of progress towards completion; and / or Professional Fellowship. Have current registration or eligibility for registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) as a medical practitioner. Demonstrate expertise and experience in teaching medical students and/or junior doctors in academia or in clinical settings. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission). Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Niru Nirthanan via email at: [email protected] or on T +617 5678 8023. For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Monday, 19 October 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
