    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000153090489": {
      "title": "Griffith University Senior Manager, Project Management Office",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Manager, Project Management Office | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Manager, Project Management Office Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Finance - FIN Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity The Senior Manager, Project Management Office is responsible for establishing, leading and continuously enhancing a divisional PMO that supports the successful delivery of Corporate Services led projects and programs. These initiatives include the University’s physical infrastructure projects, digital projects, business improvement and organisational change. The role promotes a consistent, structured and best-practice approach to project and portfolio management through the implementation of governance frameworks, delivery methodologies, portfolio planning, resource and capacity management, financial oversight, and benefits realisation processes. Working collaboratively with Corporate Services executives, senior leaders, project sponsors and delivery teams, the Senior Manager provides strategic advice, oversight and assurance to support effective decision-making, strengthen project outcomes, and ensure investments align with the University's strategic objectives and Corporate Services priorities. Key responsibilities Lead the Corporate Services PMO, ensuring effective governance, delivery standards, reporting and accountability across the project portfolio. Support project planning, prioritisation and approval processes, including business case development, benefits analysis and stage-gate reviews. Maintain an integrated portfolio roadmap, providing visibility of project schedules, resource requirements, dependencies, risks and key decision points. Provide strategic advice and reporting to the Chief Financial Officer, Executive leaders and governance forums on portfolio performance, risks, priorities and resource allocation. Deliver independent portfolio oversight and assurance by monitoring project performance, financial outcomes, risks, change readiness and benefits realisation. Recommend corrective actions and governance improvements where projects require intervention, escalation or remediation. Implement and continuously enhance PMO tools, methodologies, templates and reporting frameworks to support effective project delivery and decision-making. Drive continuous improvement through lessons learned, post-implementation reviews and project maturity initiatives across Corporate Services. About you Tertiary qualifications in project management, business, information technology, construction, engineering, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant qualifications and substantial senior leadership experience in complex project, program, or portfolio environments. Demonstrated success in establishing, leading and maturing a Project Management Office (PMO), managing complex project portfolios, or overseeing a comparable project governance and assurance function within a large, multifaceted organisation. Proven expertise in developing and implementing project governance frameworks, portfolio management practices, reporting methodologies, performance measures, and assurance processes that support the successful delivery of strategic initiatives and organisational objectives. Formal project, program, or portfolio management certification, such as PRINCE2, MSP, PMBOK, Agile, SAFe, or an equivalent industry-recognised qualification, is highly desirable. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, communication and influencing skills, with a demonstrated ability to build credibility, provide trusted advice, and influence senior executives, project sponsors and governance bodies to drive strategic outcomes, informed decision-making and organisational change. Strong commercial, financial and strategic acumen, including experience overseeing project investment decisions, resource allocation, budget management, benefits realisation and portfolio prioritisation in a complex organisational environment. Demonstrated ability to lead, coach and develop high-performing teams while fostering a culture of accountability, continuous improvement, collaboration and delivery excellence across project and business functions. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 3 years based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary An attractive salary package will be negotiated with the preferred candidate, commensurate with skills, qualifications and experience. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 18th October at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. We kindly ask recruitment agencies not to send unsolicited CVs or approach members of our hiring team regarding this role, as the recruitment process is being managed internally. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Administration Officer – Marketing and Communications Southport, Australia Operations and Compliance Officer Southport, Australia School Manager - School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work Southport, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Senior Manager, Project Management Office 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154922509": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Strategic Partnerships (Nathan or Gold Coast)",
      "description": "About the opportunity  At Griffith University, fostering impactful partnerships is fundamental. Our Industry and External Engagement (IEE) Portfolio prioritises strong relationships with industry, governments, nonprofits , and the community, driving positive social outcomes through collaborations across Queensland, Australia and globally. The Senior Manager Strategic Partnerships will work with other senior managers at the University, under the broad direction of the Director Industry and External Engagement (IEE), to achieve outcomes consistent with the objectives of the Office of the Vice President Industry and External Engagement and University Strategic Plan. This includes leading and developing a suite of multidisciplinary partnerships to build and grow Griffith’s profile and reputation and achieve University strategic goals. As a Senior Manager, Strategic Partnerships, you’ll take on complex local and global challenges, using your skills and experience to drive meaningful change. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Identify, develop and manage major strategic collaborative opportunities involving multiple partners and/or internal stakeholders, with primary responsibility for Griffith Business School and complementary coverage across Arts, Education and LawManage and develop a set of partnerships for the University with a range of stakeholders/targets, including partner liaison, partnership prospectus of ideas, proposal writing and presentations to grow current and potential partnerships that meet the University’s strategic industry partnership goals. Engage with Academic Groups to identify, develop and lead business development for impact that may span research, education and training projects and programs. Partnering with Central Portfolios (including Research, Advancement and Marketing & Communications) to progress activities including media, marketing, promotion and external relationships to align partnerships for impact. Liaise, consult and work closely with key external stakeholders to ensure synergies are optimised, and that promotion of Griffith and its unique capabilities are maximised. Provide strategic advice, expert negotiation and professional expertise in the development of all relevant partnership agreements and documentation which support the development of mutually beneficial partnership arrangements and meet legislative, University and policy requirements. About you \n \nWhat matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: Relevant postgraduate qualifications and possess substantial proven experience in business development. This includes expertise in value creation and opportunity identification, communication and collaborative relationship management, and negotiation and deal-making skills. Experience in leading strategic projects including implementing plans, managing resources, and ensure projects are delivered on time. Proficient in crafting high-level communications for diverse audiences, and ability to convey complex issues clearly and persuasively. Competent in facilitatingcollaboration agreements with legal and commercial departments. Adept in stakeholder management, leadership, and a solid understanding of higher education administration would further enhance the ability to fulfill these responsibilities effectively. Prior experience or background in the sector would be highly regarded. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing opportunity and can be based at Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary \nHEW 10 – Base - $147,057.74 + 17% superannuation. Full package is $172,057.55. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Tuesday 20th October at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Industry and External Engagement"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154915559": {
      "title": "Counsellor",
      "description": "Counselling & Wellbeing offers students, and staff, a range of support services including counselling, chaplaincy, disability and accessibility, student safety and health services. These services are voluntary, confidential, and professional, and reflect the diversity of our shared learning community. Counselling & Wellbeing also provides advice to senior officers on matters relating to student safety and wellbeing. The multi-disciplinary  Counselling & Wellbeing team are an open and welcoming group, passionate about supporting and enhancing Griffith University and its students. In this professional role, use your skills and experience to drive meaningful change, here’s how you’ll make it matter: Provide professional counselling in response to personal concerns affecting student study and life. In this short term, solution focused support, assist students to get back on track so have the best chance of success in both their personal and academic life. Liaise with other staff and stakeholders within the team and department, as well as across the wider University. Become involved in a range of initiatives, including workshops and campaigns. You will be engaging with students face to face or by telehealth - video or by phone and will have the use of a university vehicle to travel between campuses. The benefit of working in tertiary education is that is a positive environment where students are constructively working towards their goals and future.  Your support will enhance their journey. About you \nWhat matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: Demonstrated, high standard of competency in counselling service delivery (not necessarily with students), Significant postgraduate experience in individual counselling, and The ability to work effectively with a high degree of self-direction (management) in an autonomous work setting with minimal day-to-day supervision. If your background is with working for not for profit / government environments, this role would be ideal for you. What we can offer \nThis is a continuing, full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith University Logan. There is an option to work from home 2 days per week. As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. \n \n Salary Range \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be HEW 8 range $117,579- $132,273 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $137,567 - $154,759 per annum. \n\n A four-year degree or equivalent in Counselling, Social Work or other relevant area. Registered as a Psychologist (AHPRA); or Registered or eligible for registration as a Social Worker (AASW) – (Mental Health Accreditation (AMHSW) is highly valued); or Registered as a Counsellor (ACA Level 3 or 4). A Blue Card, Queensland’s working with children check, is required for this position if the occupant is not a registered health practitioner with the  Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency . If you don’t currently hold a Blue Card, you must be open to obtain one before commencing in the position. \n\n As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role referring to the Job Description and relevant Qualifications as outlined in the job advertisement. You may review the Position Description for additional information. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have Australian working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position \nSuccessful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role , please contact Russell Campbell, Head, Counselling and Wellbeing, Student Health, Counselling and Wellbeing via email:  russell.campbell@griffith.edu.au For application support contact Kate Watson, Talent Acquisition Partner via email: kate.watson@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Sunday 25 October 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Student Life"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154914149": {
      "title": "Platform Engineer - Workspace",
      "description": "Platform Engineers ensure the continued successful operation of technology platforms, minimising disruptions that may impact client experience. They are accountable for maintaining the high availability, resilience, security and performance of technology platforms and associated business operations and services, incorporating automation to improve efficiency and reduce repetitive tasks. The role performs operational activities across endpoint management and infrastructure platforms, including availability and capacity management, service support, configuration management, software deployment, upgrades, patching and security compliance. Platform Engineers support the development, implementation and ongoing management of technology solutions through configuration, installation, systems integration, testing and post-implementation support. They actively contribute to the continual improvement of Platform Engineering practices, methods, workflows and tools, ensuring technology environments remain secure, reliable and fit for purpose. Key Responsibilities Endpoint and Platform Management: Administer, configure and maintain Windows and macOS endpoint environments using Microsoft Intune, SCCM/MECM and JAMF. Maintain platform availability, device compliance, configuration standards, patching and lifecycle management while minimising service disruptions. Application Packaging and Deployment: Package, configure, test, deploy, update and remove applications using SCCM/MECM, Intune and JAMF. Ensure reliable software distribution, maintain deployment workflows and documentation, and automate provisioning and repetitive deployment activities where appropriate. Endpoint Security and Configuration Management: Implement and maintain endpoint security controls, including Microsoft Defender integration with Intune, application control, Attack Surface Reduction (ASR) rules, security policies and configuration baselines. Administer and troubleshoot Active Directory and Group Policy within a complex enterprise environment to support security, compliance and consistent endpoint configuration. Testing, Implementation and Technical Support: Design and execute test cases for applications, configurations, platform changes and system integrations. Document results, identify risks and issues, support implementation activities, troubleshoot operational problems and provide post-implementation support to ensure solutions meet technical and business requirements. Infrastructure Operations and Service Management: Maintain endpoint management infrastructure and supporting services, monitoring availability, capacity, performance, resource utilisation and service levels. Undertake upgrades, patching and maintenance, identify required changes, and contribute to operational planning and the resolution of complex technical issues. Technical Documentation, Automation and Continuous Improvement: Develop and maintain accurate technical documentation, standard operating procedures, deployment instructions, configuration records and repeatable operational workflows. Identify opportunities to improve processes, automate repetitive tasks and enhance the efficiency, consistency and reliability of platform engineering practices. Collaboration, Guidance and Operational Planning: Collaborate with technical teams and stakeholders to support technology implementations, provide technical guidance within areas of expertise, manage competing priorities and contribute to resource planning. Recognise knowledge limitations and engage appropriate expertise to resolve issues and deliver effective outcomes About You The successful applicant will hold a relevant degree with at least four years of subsequent relevant experience, or possess an equivalent combination of qualifications, training and relevant professional experience. You will demonstrate: Enterprise Endpoint Management: Proven experience administering Microsoft Intune, SCCM/MECM and JAMF in an enterprise environment, with practical expertise managing Windows and macOS devices, configurations, compliance, patching and software deployment. Application Packaging and Deployment: Demonstrated experience packaging, testing, deploying and troubleshooting applications across SCCM/MECM, Intune and JAMF, including an understanding of deployment workflows, application dependencies and reliable software distribution. Endpoint Security and Infrastructure: Strong technical skills in Microsoft Defender integration with Intune, application control, Attack Surface Reduction (ASR) rules, Active Directory and Group Policy management, with an understanding of enterprise security controls and configuration compliance. Technical Documentation and Process Improvement: Excellent documentation and workflow development skills, including creating clear, accurate and repeatable technical procedures, deployment instructions and operational documentation, with a focus on automation and continuous improvement. Technical Problem-Solving and Collaboration: Strong analytical, troubleshooting and problem-solving skills, with the ability to resolve complex technical issues, assess risks, manage competing priorities and work collaboratively with technical teams and stakeholders to deliver reliable technology services. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer \nThis is a full time, fixed term opportunity until December 2027 based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 7 Salary - Base range - $104,504.60 - $113,219.43 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $122,270.38 - $132,466.72. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 25th October at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matter most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Digital Solutions. A team you’ll want to be a part of. \nWhen you join Digital Solutions, you’ll be part of a team that delivers impact by enhancing digital experiences for the graduates of tomorrow, researchers of today and all those working to make it a brighter future.  But we know it’s not just what you do that matters, it’s who you do it with. Our people will tell you – our team sets us apart. We promise a supportive and friendly environment where you’ll collaborate to make an impact. Make it matter. Join Digital Solutions at Griffith.",
      "department": "Digital Solutions"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154913189": {
      "title": "Training & Development Officer",
      "description": "About the opportunity Reporting to the Web Manager, Marketing Technology, this role is responsible for developing and delivering engaging training, resources and capability programs that empower Griffith University's web publishing community. Working closely with web publishers, content authors and key stakeholders, you will promote best practice in web publishing, accessibility, content governance and digital content management, while supporting the successful adoption of web platform enhancements and digital transformation initiatives. Key responsibilities Identify and assess capability development needs across Griffith’s web publishing community. Develop and deliver engaging training programs, resources and support materials that promote best practice in web publishing, accessibility and content governance. Create and maintain learning content across University learning systems, knowledge bases and support channels. Support the successful adoption of web platform enhancements and digital initiatives. Evaluate training outcomes and use insights and feedback to continuously improve learning programs. Partner with stakeholders and subject matter experts to ensure training materials remain relevant, effective and up to date. Foster a culture of continuous learning, knowledge sharing and best practice across the University’s web publishing network. About you The occupant of this position will hold a degree with subsequent relevant experience in training, learning and development, digital communications, education, organisational capability development or a related discipline; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education and/or training. Experience in the development and delivery of training programs, workshops, learning resources or professional development initiatives. Experience working with enterprise digital platforms, content management systems or similar technologies is desirable. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer \nThis is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 6 months based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 6 – Base range - $94,966.18 - $101,295.51 + 17% superannuation. Full package range is $111,110.42 - $118,515.75. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 25th October at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Marketing and Communications  provide university-wide strategic marketing and communications advice and develop, manage and implement marketing and communications activities (including advertising) across all Griffith audiences including prospective and current students, staff, alumni, donors and corporate partners. Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Marketing and Communications"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154912069": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Level C) / Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing",
      "description": "The School of Nursing and Midwifery is one of the largest of schools within the Heath Group and Griffith University. Our School has a strong international reputation (ranked #1 in Australia, #6 in the world, 2026 Shanghai ranking), and we are committed to the global development of nursing and midwifery practice, theory and research in positive and visionary ways. The school is seeking to appoint a Senior Lecturer (Level C) or Associate Professor (Level D) in nursing at Griffith University Gold Coast. As a Senior Lecturer (Level C) Nursing, you will contribute to both teaching and research in the school. You will teach and convene courses in undergraduate and postgraduate programs, supervise Honours and Higher Research Degree students, and undertake high impact research aligned with the research strengths of the school. Where required, this position will also act as program coordinator and/or other leadership roles.  In this role, you will: Lead and innovate in nursing education, designing engaging learning experiences that prepare students for contemporary healthcare practice. Conduct and lead impactful research that advances nursing knowledge, influences practice and contributes to improved health outcomes. Provide academic leadership and mentorship, supporting colleagues, research students, and the ongoing development of the nursing discipline. Build strong industry and community partnerships that enhance student opportunities, strengthen workforce connections, and create real-world impact. Drive excellence across teaching, research, and service, contributing to the School’s strategic priorities and reputation as a leader in nursing education. As an Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing , you will also contribute to excellence in teaching, research and academic leadership within the school, driving innovative education and impactful research that strengthens the nursing profession and improves health outcomes. In this role, you will: Lead and conduct high quality research that aligns with the School’s research strengths, attracts competitive funding, and delivers meaningful impact for healthcare policy, practice and communities. Teach and convene courses across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing programs, creating engaging, student-centred learning experiences that support student success and employability. Supervise and mentor Honours, Higher Degree Research (HDR) and postgraduate students, fostering research excellence and developing the next generation of nursing scholars and leaders. Provide academic leadership through program coordination and other leadership responsibilities, contributing to curriculum innovation, quality enhancement and the strategic direction of the School. Build and strengthen collaborations with academic, industry and healthcare partners to enhance research impact, support workforce development and elevate the School’s reputation nationally and internationally. This is a continuing, full-time position based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range Senior Lecturer (Level C) Nursing \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level C range $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level D range $172,686 - $190,248 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $202,043 - $222,590 per annum. \n \nFurther to this salary package the School of Nursing and Midwifery are willing to support the right candidate with a range of additional benefits including: Start-up funds Relocation Support (if required) Visa Sponsorship (if required) \n\n To be successful in this role, you will have: Senior Lecturer Level C Hold a PhD in Nursing or a related discipline, together with unrestricted registration as a Registered Nurse with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra). Evidence of a research track record and demonstratable commitment to teaching excellence, including course coordination and curriculum development. You will have proven success in attracting competitive research grant funding and a track record of publishing high-quality papers, attracting competitive research grant funding, and publishing. Desirable expertise as either an Ahpra endorsement to prescribe as a registered nurse/nurse practitioner, or Infection Prevention and Control or Mental Health or Aged Care nursing. Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing  In addition to the above, you will have: Demonstrate an established research track record, including publication in high-quality peer reviewed journals, success in securing competitive research funding, and evidence of research impact at a national and/or international level. Possess a strong record of teaching excellence in higher education, with experience in curriculum design, course convening, program coordination, and the delivery of innovative, evidence-based learning experiences. Show a proven ability to supervise and mentor Honours and Higher Degree Research (HDR) candidates to successful completion, while contributing to the development of a vibrant research culture. Bring highly developed leadership, collaboration and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build productive partnerships across academic, healthcare, industry and professional communities. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to Apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details, education or qualification history, employment history including present position and details of relevant professional, consulting or industry experience, evidence of recent academic teaching evaluations, research interests with list of publications, research grants awarded and other relevant information, such as offices held in professional bodies, community services etc. Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) VISA Sponsorship will be available to the successful candidate. For further information about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner, Head of School at hos.sonm@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday, 22 November at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n At Griffith University we believe in, strive for and celebrate the remarkable. We are known for our high impact research, outstanding student experience, our commitment to social justice, and our welcoming environment. We rank in the top 2% of universities worldwide, and we're proud of our remarkable achievements, of our people, and their passion for making a positive difference. Together we contribute to the development of knowledge and learning in an attractive environment which values excellence, equity, diversity, and innovation.",
      "department": "School of Nursing and Midwifery"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154585849": {
      "title": "Placement Officer",
      "description": "Join a team that helps shape the next generation of allied health, sport and social work professionals. At Griffith University, we are looking for an exceptional administrator to join our Placement Team as a Placement Officer. If you are highly organised, tech-savvy, enjoy building relationships and delivering excellent customer service, this could be the perfect opportunity for you. In this role, you will coordinate student placements, support compliance and preparation activities, manage records and systems, and work closely with students, academics and industry partners to ensure positive placement experiences. Previous placement experience is welcome but not required. We provide comprehensive training and value strong organisational skills, attention to detail, adaptability and confidence using technology. Our team is known for its supportive culture, strong collaboration and commitment to professional growth. You will be welcomed into a dynamic environment where your contribution is valued and where ongoing learning and development are encouraged. In this role, you will: Coordinate the allocation, administration and ongoing management of student placements across relevant programs and disciplines. Support students through placement preparation, pre-placement requirements, compliance processes, correspondence and practical advice. Work closely with academic leads, professional staff and placement colleagues to deliver high-quality placement experiences. Develop and maintain positive relationships with industry partners, including supporting new and recurring placement opportunities and placement deed administration. Use placement or education management systems to maintain records, monitor requirements, prepare reports and support quality assurance, evaluation and accreditation activities. Contribute to operational activities including databases, orientation materials, assessments, finance processes, supervisor engagement and payment administration, events and continuous improvement initiatives. About You You will bring relevant experience, training and/or qualifications, supported by strong organisational skills, sound judgement and clear communication. Experience in student administration, placements, compliance, health education, partner engagement or complex service environments would be highly regarded. You will also demonstrate: Ability to build strong professional relationships with students, staff and external partners. Is proactive, adaptable, resilient and solution-focused in a changing environment. Can balance competing priorities, manage details accurately and work with a high level of independence. Is digitally confident and comfortable using systems, data and records to support effective placement administration. Values teamwork, contributes positively to culture and is committed to student success, continuous improvement and professional growth. This is a continuing, full-time position primarily based at Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 5 range $82,415 - $92,456 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $96,426 - $108,174 per annum. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Elise Bailey, Placement and Partnerships Team Leader at e.bailey@griffith.edu.au \n \nFor application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au            Closing date: Sunday, 1 November 2026 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every student deserves the opportunity to turn learning into real-world experience. At Griffith University, placements and Work Integrated Learning are a critical part of preparing the next generation of health and human services professionals. They connect our students with industry, communities and the professions they will ultimately join. The Griffith School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work brings together a diverse range of disciplines committed to improving the health and wellbeing of individuals and communities. Supporting this work is a dedicated placements team responsible for creating and coordinating high-quality placement experiences for our students and building strong partnerships with the organisations that support them.",
      "department": "School of Health Sciences and Social Work"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154330387": {
      "title": "Service Centre Supervisor (IT)",
      "description": "About the Opportunity Lead and coordinate customer focused and specialist IT support services that underpin end‑user computing and teaching technologies across the University. You’ll be responsible for delivering reliable, responsive, and scalable support for staff, students, and teaching environments overseeing incident and request management, service performance, and continuous improvement. Working within a service aligned model, you’ll drive strong customer outcomes, uphold service standards, and build team capability to meet University priorities. Key Responsibilities Lead day-to-day delivery of end-user computing, AV, collaboration, and Service Centre support services. Coordinate incidents, requests, and service tasks to meet agreed SLAs and standards. Supervise and develop technical staff, managing workloads, performance, and team capability. Drive continuous improvement of end-user and teaching technology services. Provide senior technical guidance and escalation support for complex issues. Support peak periods, semester readiness, and technology rollouts. Collaborate with service leads, projects, and partners to deliver integrated outcomes. Monitor performance, trends, and feedback to improve service quality and user experience. Maintain clear procedures, documentation, and knowledge resources. Support device lifecycle management, including deployment, maintenance, and decommissioning. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant tertiary qualifications with subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing opportunity based as Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 7 – Base range - $104,504.60 - $113,219.43 17% super. Full package range - $122,270.38 - $132,466.72. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Open until filled. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
