    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000157254300": {
      "title": "Griffith University Scientific Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: HTS - Anatomy Facility - ANF Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Technical Partners Health (TPH) is an essential provision of technical support crossing the whole of Griffith Health , spanning across three integral streams: Technologies, Operations and Logistics (TOL) Laboratory and Preclinical Experience Simulation and Practical Experience Our team of 50+ technical specialists supports teaching, research, clinics, and learning within purpose-built facilities across multiple campuses. Job Description An exciting opportunity exists for a Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology to join our Anatomy Facilities team. Reporting to the Anatomy Facility Manager, you will play a critical role in supporting anatomy and pathology teaching, research, and laboratory operations. This position provides specialist technical expertise to academics, researchers, and students while ensuring the highest standards of laboratory practice, compliance, and operational excellence. In this role, you will: Prepare, embalm, maintain and catalogue human anatomical and pathology specimens to support teaching, research and outreach activities. Undertake cadaveric dissections and prepare high-quality anatomical prosections for educational purposes. Provide specialist technical support to academic staff, researchers and students within anatomy and pathology facilities. Coordinate the day-to-day operation of laboratories, including equipment maintenance, resource management and laboratory scheduling. Support the administration and delivery of the Body Donation Program, ensuring activities are conducted in accordance with legislative, ethical and university requirements. Maintain accurate records, databases and documentation relating to specimens, laboratory operations and compliance activities. Deliver laboratory inductions, safety training and technical guidance to staff and students. Ensure compliance with workplace health and safety requirements, risk management processes and relevant legislation. Assist with the procurement, monitoring and maintenance of laboratory equipment, consumables and resources. Support the preparation and delivery of Physiology practical sessions, including set-up, pack-down, and coordination of consumables procurement and inventory management. Liaise professionally with funeral directors, external organisations, donors' families, suppliers and other stakeholders. Contribute to outreach activities, workshops, facility tours and other initiatives that promote anatomy and pathology education. Support continuous improvement initiatives to enhance laboratory operations, service delivery and the overall student and researcher experience. About you You are a highly organised and adaptable technical professional with a passion for supporting excellence in education and research. You are comfortable working in a specialist anatomical environment and possess strong interpersonal skills that enable you to collaborate effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. To be successful in this role, you will bring: A health-related degree with relevant practical experience, or an equivalent combination of qualifications, training and demonstrated expertise. Experience working with human and other biological materials, including knowledge of cadaveric dissection and embalming techniques. Demonstrated laboratory, technical or scientific support experience within a teaching, research, health, or clinical environment. Strong organisational skills with the ability to coordinate multiple priorities and maintain accurate records. Knowledge of laboratory safety practices, risk management processes, and relevant legislation. Excellent communication skills and a commitment to providing high-quality support and service. Confidence using a range of digital systems, databases, and laboratory technologies. This is a full time, continuing position based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time base salary for a HEW Level 5 is in the range $82,415 - $92,456 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total FTE package is in the range $96,426- $108,174 per annum. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Opportunities for internal mobility How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the job description and the position description ). Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details. Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact James Ashaolu, Anatomy Facility Manager (TPH), at j.ashaolu@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Monday, 23rd November at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast) Nathan, Australia Student Connect Officer Nathan, Australia Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing Brisbane, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology Kessels Rd, MacGregor QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000157037000": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Nursing and Midwifery - Nursing - NUR Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Lead the Future of Acute Care Nursing – Joint Appointment Senior Research Fellow with Griffith University and Princess Alexandra Hospital . Griffith University is a progressive, values-led university dedicated to learning, leadership, and innovation. This is your chance to help us achieve our vision to transform lives and add to human knowledge and understanding in a way that creates a future that benefits all. The Griffith School of Nursing and Midwifery is internationally recognised for excellence in education and research. It is consistently ranked among the world’s leading nursing and midwifery schools (#1 in Australia, #6 in the world; 2026 Shanghai Ranking by Academic Subjects). We are committed to advancing practice, policy and research that improves health outcomes for all. Princess Alexandra Hospital (PAH) is a tertiary health care centre, providing care in all major adult specialties to patients throughout Queensland and Australia, except for obstetrics. We are one of Australia’s leading academic and research health centres, providing Clinical Service Capability Framework (CSCF) Level 6 services, with approximately 1,000 beds. PAH is nationally recognised for expertise in trauma management, and we are a major transplantation centre for livers, kidneys, bone, cartilage, and corneas. We also have responsibility for a number of state-wide services including Queensland Liver Transplant Service, Queensland Tissue Bank, Queensland Spinal Cord Injury Service. The ICU is undergoing a major expansion.  The PAH fulfils a significant teaching and research role, undertaking research and educational programs with affiliated universities and institutes. The expanding research profile is characterised by its full spectrum from basic science to clinical care. Job Description Are you ready to shape the next generation of Acute Care Nurses and lead transformative research at a global scale? Griffith University and Princess Alexandra Hospital are seeking a visionary leader to drive innovation, education, and research in Acute Care Nursing through a prestigious joint appointment. We invite applications from outstanding Acute care nursing leaders for a joint appointment as Senior Research Fellow of Acute Care Nursing. This prestigious role will suit a highly regarded academic and clinician who is passionate about advancing acute care nursing research, education and evidence-based practice through strong clinical- academic collaboration. This is a fixed term, full-time position for three years based in Brisbane at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) and Princess Alexandra Hospital. The successful candidate will be required to work across both locations in person as a requirement of the role. Griffith University's sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be $143,418 - $165,374 per annum plus 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Qualifications To be successful in this role, you will have excellent communication and interpersonal skills with a demonstrated and extensive commitment to higher education and nursing. In addition, the successful applicant will demonstrate: Possession of a doctoral qualification or equivalent professional experience in nursing or a relevant field. Registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra) as a registered nurse which is to be active and maintained for the duration of the appointment. A demonstrated track-record in the ability to attract external competitive research funding, to supervise research students and to build and lead multidisciplinary research teams in Acute Care Nursing. Additional Information How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following: A cover letter addressing your suitability for the position (refer to listed qualifications and position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details detailing your academic and professional history Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. Important Information for Applicants Evidence of vaccination (or the ability to be vaccinated) against the following is required: Measles, Mumps, Rubella, Varicella, Pertussis, and Hepatitis B. Tuberculosis screening may be required to determine vaccination needs. Any serious disciplinary history must be disclosed. For further information about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner – Head of School, School of Nursing and Midwifery on [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Thursday, 26 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000156463939": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "Griffith University Research Fellow - Ultrafast/Strong-Field/Attosecond Science | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Research Fellow - Ultrafast/Strong-Field/Attosecond Science Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Environment and Science - ESC Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity We are seeking a talented and motivated Research Fellow to join a leading research team undertaking pioneering work in ultrafast, strong-field and attosecond science. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to internationally recognised research at the forefront of understanding electron dynamics and chemical processes on attosecond timescales. Working collaboratively with world-class researchers, you will play a key role in the Australian Research Council Discovery Project, \"Attochemistry – Imaging Valence Electrons in Motion\" Through the design and delivery of innovative experiments, you will help advance fundamental knowledge of electron behaviour during chemical transformations, contributing to high-impact research outcomes and strengthening Griffith University's reputation for research excellence. This is an exciting opportunity to access state-of-the-art facilities, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to breakthrough discoveries in a rapidly evolving field of science. Key responsibilities Conduct high-quality research that advances the objectives of the research program, contributing to innovative discoveries and impactful outcomes within the Centre and associated projects. Develop a strong research profile through the publication of findings in leading international peer-reviewed journals and by contributing to the development of competitive research funding applications. Collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams, providing expertise and contributing to a broad range of research initiatives aligned with the Centre's priorities. Prepare and deliver high-quality research outputs, including publications, conference presentations, technical reports and stakeholder communications. Contribute to teaching, student learning and curriculum activities as required, supporting Griffith University's commitment to academic excellence. Support the supervision, mentoring and development of Higher Degree Research (HDR) candidates, fostering a positive and productive research environment. Provide guidance and oversight to Research Assistants and technical staff to ensure the successful delivery of research objectives. Maintain compliance with all relevant legislation, ethical requirements, laboratory standards, and University policies and procedures, while promoting a safe, inclusive and professional research culture. About you The occupant of this position will hold a PhD or equivalent qualifications/work experience in Ultrafast/Strong-Field/Attosecond science or a related field. Candidates with prior post-doctoral research experience and hands-on operational knowledge of intense ultrafast lasers and/or photon/particle detectors will be favoured. Sponsorship may be offered for the right candidate. What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term opportunity until 30/09/2029 based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Research Fellow Grade 2 – Base range - $117,076.11 - $139,031.71 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $136,979.05 - $162,667.11. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For further specifics on this role and its responsibilities please reach out to Professor Igor Litvinyuk on [email protected] For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] Closing date: Tuesday 3rd November at 11:59pm All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000156428385": {
      "title": "Griffith University Scientific Officer (Chemistry)",
      "description": "Griffith University Scientific Officer (Chemistry) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Scientific Officer (Chemistry) Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Environment and Science - ESC Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity We are currently looking for a Scientific Officer (Chemistry) to support teaching and research in the School of Environment and Science’s South Brisbane laboratories. The position will be primarily supporting teaching activities and, on occasion, also assisting research facilities and engagement activities. The role also includes the upkeep of laboratory documentation and assisting with H&S compliance. As a Scientific Officer (Chemistry), you will take on complex challenges, using your skills and experience to drive meaningful change. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Provide technical and operational support for teaching, e.g., planning; set-up; refreshing; pre-running; using and demonstrating equipment; and dismantling of experiments for teaching laboratories. Perform regular calibration, minor maintenance and service scheduling of all relevant instrumentation and equipment. Provide training and supervision of Scientific Assistants, Attendants and Casual staff when they are assigned to the area that is within the remit of the Scientific Officer’s responsibility. Provide technical assistance, including advice on sample preparation, to Griffith University staff and students, and representatives from external organisations as directed by Technical & Core Facility Manager. Support ESC outreach and community engagement events and activities as directed by the line managers. About you What matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: A degree in Science majoring in Chemistry and relevant practical experience, or an equivalent combination of education, skills and experience. Strong laboratory and technical skills, including the ability to plan, set up, operate, and maintain chemistry experiments and equipment in a teaching and research environment. Demonstrated experience in risk assessment and laboratory safety, particularly in the handling of chemicals, biological reagents, and scientific instrumentation. Excellent documentation and organisational skills, with the ability to develop clear procedures, resource statements, and operational protocols. Proven ability to lead, train, and support technical staff, as well as provide expert assistance to students, academics, and external stakeholders. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing opportunity based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 5 - Base range - $82,415.66 - $92,456.55 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $96,426.31 - $108,174.16. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acqusition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Tuesday 3rd November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology MacGregor, Australia Research Fellow - Ultrafast/Strong-Field/Attosecond Science Nathan, Australia Training Manager - ARC Training Centre for Climate-Resilient Water Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Scientific Officer (Chemistry) 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000156201129": {
      "title": "Griffith University Principal Internal Auditor",
      "description": "Griffith University Principal Internal Auditor | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Principal Internal Auditor Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Risk and Compliance - ARC Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity Operating under the broad direction of the Associate Director, Internal Audit, the Principal Internal Auditor provides strategic leadership across the University's internal audit, assurance, risk and governance functions. The role leads and completes  complex, organisation-wide assurance reviews and delivers independent, expert advice to the University Executive, and senior leaders on governance, risk management, internal controls and emerging strategic issues. Exercising a high degree of professional independence, the position plays a critical role in strengthening governance practices, enhancing organisational performance, and supporting the achievement of the University's strategic objectives. Key responsibilities Work autonomously to deliver a portfolio of complex, enterprise-wide audit and assurance reviews, providing independent insights and recommendations that strengthen governance, risk management, compliance and organisational performance. Partner with senior leaders to identify emerging risks, evaluate internal controls and drive continuous improvement across the University's operations, systems and strategic initiatives. Provide expert advice on governance, risk and assurance matters, influencing decision-making and supporting the effective achievement of strategic objectives. Prepare and present high-quality audit reports and recommendations to senior executives  and monitor the implementation of agreed actions. Contribute to the enhancement of the University's governance and risk frameworks, leveraging data-driven insights to improve organisational effectiveness and build capability across the institution. About you Relevant tertiary qualifications in accounting, finance, business or a related discipline, together with CPA or CA membership. Significant experience leading internal audit, risk and compliance reviews within a Chartered Accounting, professional services or complex organisational environment. Deep knowledge of contemporary internal auditing, risk management, governance frameworks and financial controls. Strong understanding of internal audit standards and best practice, including the Institute of Internal Auditors (IIA) Global Internal Audit Standards. Professional membership of the Institute of Internal Auditors (IIA) and/or Certified Internal Auditor (CIA) qualification will be highly regarded. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing opportunity based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 10 – Base salary - $147,057.74 + 17% superannuation. Full package - $172,057.55. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 1st November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University The Susan McClary Research Fellowship in Musicology South Brisbane, Australia Senior Manager, Corporate Governance Nathan, Australia Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast) Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Principal Internal Auditor 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000156200779": {
      "title": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women",
      "description": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: DVC Research - SDV Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description The ARC Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women (CEVAW) is the world’s first centre to tackle the full range of forms of violence against women in Australia and the Indo-Pacific region. CEVAW aims to transform our understanding of the problem by: examining the structural drivers that cause and compound violence against women (VAW) pioneering new, evidence-based approaches to inform trajectory-altering practice and policy. CEVAW will generate fundamental knowledge on the causes of violence, the contexts in which it occurs, and the most effective and efficient responses. This interdisciplinary research will be data-driven, Indigenous-centred and co-designed with partners. CEVAW brings together more than 40 world-leading experts to develop scalable approaches to eliminate violence against women across the legal, security, economic, health and political systems of Australia and the region. By building strategic and strong partnerships with Australian and international research institutions and partner organisations, CEVAW will translate research into innovative tools and strengthened capacity to drive the elimination of violence against women. Located at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus, Griffith University. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Job Description The ARC Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women is seeking a highly motivated PhD candidate to join our team and contribute to a significant research project focusing on conflict-related sexual violence (CRSV) in the Indo-Pacific. This project intends to analyse non-legal pathways to survivor-centred justice for CRSV survivors in post-conflict contexts in the Indo-Pacific. Across the region, transitional justice and reparative programs have been enacted with the intention of meeting survivors’ needs, rights, agency, and participation through different programs, including artistic and creative, faith-based, counselling, healthcare, compensation and economic empowerment, restorative justice and mediation. We welcome research project proposals that propose to explore transitional justice and reparative programs in one post-conflict context.  Proposals can also focus on historical contexts (such as the so-called ‘comfort women’ system established and controlled by the Japanese Imperial Army during World War II), contemporary conflicts (including Nepal, the Solomon Islands, Sri Lanka, Timore-Leste, and Vietnam), and frontier wars that have completed or are undergoing truth and reconciliation processes, such as the Yoorrook Justice Commission (Victoria, Australia). For Indigenous Australians interested in this project, there is an opportunity to apply for the Griffith University Indigenous Australian Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUIAPRS), which offers financial support through the provision of a stipend to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander research candidates while they undertake a higher degree research program at Griffith University. The project will suit a candidate with an interest in conflict-related sexual violence, transitional justice, human rights, gender and feminist scholarship.  The project will be designed and informed by the CEVAW's four Indigenous research principles: relationships, material benefit, equity, and Indigenous leadership. All scholarship recipients will be located with the Griffith University Node of the ARC Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women (CEVAW), under the supervision of Professor Sara Davies, Deputy Director (Indo-Pacific Research) and Dr Phyu Phyu Oo, Research Fellow, CEVAW. There will be an additional opportunity for associate supervision from one of the CEVAW Chief Investigators located in five additional CEVAW nodes (Monash University, Curtin University, Australian National University, Macquarie University and University of Melbourne). The PhD candidates will benefit from unique supervision and mentoring opportunities afforded by CEVAW’s Chief Investigators across different Australian universities as well as networking opportunities across academia and industry through conferences and CEVAW’s partner organisations, nationally and internationally. Qualifications The selection of the applicant for the award of a Higher Degree Research Scholarship at Griffith University is based on academic merit and research background. To be successful in this particular role, you will also need to demonstrate: Evidence of conflict-related sexual violence research, advocacy, or practitioner expertise (essential) Experience with mixed or multiple methods research (essential) Expressions of interest are welcome from Australian or New Zealand citizens or Australian permanent residents. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer here . Please note : Prior experience with field research in the Indo-Pacific region including Australia and Aotearoa New Zealand (desirable) Authorship on journal publications and/or reports  (desirable) Additional Information About the scholarship The value of the stipend scholarship is $36,000 per annum (full-time, fixed rate) for three years, with the option for an additional CEVAW top up scholarship of $10,000 per annum. For Indigenous Australians interested in this project, there is an opportunity to apply for the Griffith University Indigenous Australian Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUIAPRS). A full-time GUIAPRS carries an annual stipend of $55,379 (2026 rate), with the option for a CEVAW stipend of $10,000 per annum. What Griffith offers As a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EoI process Please do not select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to Professor Sara Davies sara.davies@griffith.edu.au containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal outlining your proposed research question, a brief literature review on CRSV and non-legal justice pathways and proposed mixed method research design in one more or more conflict affected contexts (1000 words). A writing sample as lead author or co-author (e.g. published paper, thesis, report) Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) using the Griffith CV template . Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is: 30 November 2026 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line Further information For project related enquiries please contact: Professor Sara Davies Phone: (07) 3735 9785 Email: sara.davies@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: Griffith Graduate Research School Email: hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Offshore Hybrid Renewable Energy Systems (OHRES): Market-Driven Site Selection and System Integration (Blue Economy CRC) Southport, Australia PhD Scholarships: Machine Vision Nathan, Australia PhD Scholarship:  Validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    }
  },
